== Recommendation 2: Fix #set Execution Guard (P0) ==

=== Problem ===
`#set` parser function executes even when validation fails, creating invalid SMW data.

=== Solution ===
Move all `#set` calls inside Lua validation success block only.

=== Implementation ===

'''Before (Current):'''
```mediawiki
{{#if: {{{Title|}}} | 
  {{#if: {{{Definition|}}} |
    {{#set: Has title = {{{Title|}}} }}  <!-- Still executes if Title exists -->
  | {{Error|Missing Definition}} }}
| {{Error|Missing Title}} }}
```

'''After (Fixed):'''
```lua
-- In Module:InfoboxValidator
function p.concept(frame)
    local args = frame.args
    local base = require("Module:ValidatorBase")

    -- Validate FIRST
    local valid, missing = base.validate_required(args, {"title", "definition", "domain"})
    if not valid then
        return base.render_error(missing)
    end

    -- Only NOW generate SMW
    local smw = "{{#set:"
    smw = smw .. "|Has title=" .. args.title
    smw = smw .. "|Has definition=" .. args.definition
    smw = smw .. "|Has domain=" .. args.domain
    smw = smw .. "}}"

    return smw .. render_infobox_html(args)
end
```

=== Risk Assessment ===
* '''Risk:''' Medium - changes SMW data generation timing
* '''Mitigation:''' Test with existing pages to ensure properties still set
* '''Rollback:''' Immediate revert if SMW queries break

