== Recommendation 3: Enforce Controlled Vocabularies (P1) ==

=== Problem ===
Controlled vocabularies documented in TemplateData but not enforced in template code.

=== Solution ===
Centralize vocabularies in Lua module and validate all inputs.

=== Implementation ===

'''Step 1: Define Vocabularies'''
```lua
-- In Module:ValidatorBase
local CONTROLLED_VOCABS = {
    epistemic_status = {
        values = {["Hypothetical"]=1, ["Provisional"]=2, ["Established"]=3, ["Deprecated"]=4},
        default = "Provisional"
    },
    concept_type = {
        values = {["Theory"]=true, ["Model"]=true, ["Framework"]=true, ["Principle"]=true, ["Pattern"]=true},
        default = nil
    }
}

function p.get_vocab(name)
    return CONTROLLED_VOCABS[name]
end
```

'''Step 2: Validate in Template'''
```lua
function p.validate_concept_type(value)
    local vocab = CONTROLLED_VOCABS.concept_type
    if not value then return true, nil end  -- optional
    if vocab.values[value] then return true, value end
    return false, "Invalid concept_type. Valid: " .. table.concat(vocab.values, ", ")
end
```

'''Step 3: Add SMW Constraints'''
```smw
[[Has concept type::]]
[[Allows value::Theory]]
[[Allows value::Model]]
[[Allows value::Framework]]
[[Allows value::Principle]]
[[Allows value::Pattern]]
```

=== Risk Assessment ===
* '''Risk:''' Low - prevents bad data entry
* '''Mitigation:''' Allow migration period for existing pages
* '''Rollback:''' Remove SMW constraints if needed

