== Recommendation 4: Implement Relationship Field Specification (P1) ==

=== Problem ===
Relationship fields use comma-separated values without type pairing, creating ambiguity.

=== Solution ===
Use structured format: `PageName[relationship_type]`

=== Implementation ===

'''New Format:'''
```mediawiki
{{Infobox_Concept
| title = Machine Learning
| definition = ...
| domain = CS
| related_concepts = Neural Networks[part-of], Deep Learning[extends], Statistics[depends-on]
}}
```

'''Lua Parser:'''
```lua
function p.parse_relationships(rel_string)
    local rels = {}
    for entry in rel_string:gmatch("([^,]+)") do
        entry = entry:gsub("^%s+", ""):gsub("%s+$", "")
        local page, rel_type = entry:match("^(.-)%s*%[(.-)%]$")
        if page then
            table.insert(rels, {page=page, type=rel_type})
        else
            table.insert(rels, {page=entry, type="related-to"})  -- default
        end
    end
    return rels
end
```

'''SMW Generation:'''
```lua
for _, rel in ipairs(rels) do
    smw = smw .. "[[Has relationship to::" .. rel.page .. "]]"
    smw = smw .. "[[Has relationship type::" .. rel.type .. "]]"
end
```

=== Risk Assessment ===
* '''Risk:''' Medium - changes parameter format
* '''Mitigation:''' Support both old and new formats during transition
* '''Migration:''' Bot to update existing pages

